  "fashion": {
    "Overview": "Among men, the Lao traditionally wear a Khmer style billowed trouser or sampot, a Mandarin collar jacket or Indochinese shirt, and a pha biang or checkered shawl. For women, the traditional dress is a skirt with a embroidered foot called a sinh, a matching pha biang or shawl (longer shawls called hom are worn in colder areas), and is worn with a French inspired blouse. Men and women wear religious amulets, and amounts of gold and silver jewelry which is believed to ward off evil. Among Lao Theung, cotton materials are used."
